pected\": \"Status LED anodes need a supply path, such as a 3.3V rail or a switched 3.3V feed. The sibling net /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV is driven by U34.4, which suggests a corresponding source was expected for this net.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV : D28.2(A,passive) D29.2(A,passive) D30.3(A1,input) D8.2(A,passive) Q10.1(G,input) R58.2(2,passive) U34.4(Y,output) U7.5(OE,input)\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The ethernet and PI activity LEDs (D4, D14, D23) would never light, because their anodes are not connected to any supply.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"R43 is specified as 75m (0.075 ohm) even though its MPN and sister resistors R41/R42/R44 are 75 ohm, a clear wrong-value deviation in the snubber/damping network. The LEDs on /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW also have no supply source, which is a lower-confidence open-connection candidate.\"\n}",
